## S 5c. Profile Verify (after original_post)

🚨 S 5b returns `submitted: true` once the Post button click fires — this does NOT confirm the post landed. Threads silently drops original posts on auth/rate hiccups. Always verify on profile before incrementing the counter.

```bash
# 1. Navigate to profile
exec curl -s -X POST http://localhost:3847/api/browser/{{browser_profile}}/navigate -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -d '{"url":"https://www.threads.net/@{{handle_slug}}"}' 2>&1

# 2. Verify the first post on the profile matches the published text (first 30 chars, lowercased + whitespace-collapsed)
exec curl -s -X POST http://localhost:3847/api/browser/{{browser_profile}}/evaluate -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -d @- <<'ENDJSON'
{"fn":"async () => { await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, 4000)); var firstLink = document.querySelector('a[href*=\"/post/\"]'); if (!firstLink) return { verified: false, reason: 'no_posts_on_profile' }; var container = firstLink.closest('div'); while (container && container.innerText.length < 50 && container.parentElement) container = container.parentElement; var snippet = container ? container.innerText.slice(0, 400) : ''; var expected = window.__data.expectedFirst30; return { verified: snippet.toLowerCase().replace(/\\s+/g, ' ').includes(expected), firstHref: firstLink.getAttribute('href'), snippet }; }", "data": {"expectedFirst30": "FIRST_30_CHARS_LOWERCASE_COLLAPSED"}}
ENDJSON
```

`expectedFirst30` = first 30 chars of the published post, lowercased with whitespace collapsed. If `verified: false`, retry once after 8s before declaring failure.
